---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const RIVERSIDE_URL = 'https://affiliate.riverside.com/rr-video-toolkit';
const BEEHIIV_URL = 'https://www.beehiiv.com/?via=rr-post';
const PLAYBOOK_URL = 'https://start.redefiningretirement.io/guides/gen-exit-playbook';
---

<Layout
  title="Start Your Own 60-Day Video Challenge | Redefining Retirement"
  description="The free video toolkit: the daily workflow, the tools, and the AI prompts I used to post a video a day for 60 days."
  type="article"
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container ty-container">
      <img src="/images/resources/video-toolkit-cover.svg" alt="The 60-Day Video Challenge cover" class="ty-cover" width="724" height="1024" />
      <p class="ty-eyebrow">You're in. Here's your toolkit.</p>
      <h1 class="ty-headline">Start Your Own 60-Day Video Challenge</h1>
      <p class="ty-subhead">The tools I used to post a video a day for 60 days, and how to start your own. Bookmark this page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="section vt-body">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose">

        <p class="disclosure">Heads up: some links below are affiliate links. If you use them, I may earn a small commission at no cost to you.</p>

        <h2>The idea</h2>
        <p>Pick a hobby or niche you care about. Give yourself a challenge with an end date, like 30 or 60 days. Post short videos and start building an audience that's yours.</p>
        <p>That's it. Below is how I did mine, the routine, the tools, and how to set up your own.</p>

        <h2>What I did</h2>
        <p>From Aug 11 to Oct 11, 2026, I posted one video a day for 60 days. Each one took 30 to 60 minutes, start to finish.</p>
        <p>I did it on a side channel I started from zero. It added up to about 219K views across TikTok, Facebook, Instagram, and YouTube.</p>
        <p>I'm not a video guy. I just found a routine I could repeat on a tired Tuesday. Here it is.</p>

        <h2>Step 0: Pick your thing</h2>
        <p>Choose a hobby or niche you could talk about every day without forcing it. Something you already do, know, or can't shut up about. Fishing, woodworking, guitar, old cars, gardening, your day job, whatever.</p>
        <p>Don't overthink it. You're not picking forever. You're picking for the next 30 or 60 days.</p>
        <p>Stuck? Use the "help me pick my niche" prompt in the AI section below.</p>

        <h2>Start your own challenge</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Pick 30 or 60 days.</strong> Put the start and end dates on the calendar.</li>
          <li><strong>Post most days.</strong> Not perfect. Most.</li>
          <li><strong>Never skip your best day.</strong> For me that was Sunday. Find yours and protect it.</li>
          <li><strong>Track weekly.</strong> Once a week, write down followers, views, and email signups. Just three numbers.</li>
          <li><strong>Set up your email list on day 1.</strong> Not day 45. Every view from day 1 on is a chance to get an email.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The daily workflow</h2>

        <h3>1. Brain dump the idea</h3>
        <p>Talk it out or type it out. Messy is fine. Don't edit yet. Just get it out of your head.</p>

        <h3>2. Let AI pick the hook, points, and ask</h3>
        <p>I paste the brain dump into an AI assistant (I use Grok Bot). It picks the best hook, 2 or 3 talking points, and one short call to action. That's the whole script.</p>

        <h3>3. Record in Riverside</h3>
        <p>I record on the Riverside mobile app. It uploads to the cloud on its own, so the video is waiting for me in the Riverside browser app when I sit down to finish it.</p>
        <p>Most of the editing was done for me by Magic Episodes. It's a template you set up once. It runs AI cleanup before you start editing: adds your captions style, removes pauses and filler words, smooths the cuts, finds fluff, and cleans up the sound with Magic Audio, plus a few other options. I just do the final touches.</p>

        <h3>4. Publish from one place</h3>
        <p>From Riverside's export window I post straight to Instagram and TikTok and schedule for prime times. Then I push it to YouTube with a title, description, and tags.</p>
        <p>Post on Sundays if you can. Mine did best on Sundays.</p>

        <h3>5. Keep the call to action tiny</h3>
        <p>"Join my list, link in bio." That's it.</p>
        <p>Long pitches flopped. Every time. The short one got 4 signups in 4 days.</p>

        <h3>6. Collect emails in Beehiiv</h3>
        <p>Views are nice. Emails are yours. The platforms can change the rules any day. Your list stays put. Beehiiv also lets you run ads to grow it when you're ready.</p>

        <div class="side-note">
          <p class="side-note-label">Side note: my video coach</p>
          <p>Early on, I set up a Grok Bot agent as my video coach. While I brainstormed, I dumped my raw thoughts into it. It picked the best hooks, the call to action, and a basic outline.</p>
          <p>That's when things changed. Once I started using it every day, my views and engagement started going up. I still had to show up and hit record. But I stopped guessing at the opening line.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>The tools, and how to get started</h2>

        <div class="tool-card">
          <h3>Riverside</h3>
          <p>Recording, cleanup, captions, and publishing, all in one spot. This is the one that saved me the most time.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Sign up, then install the Riverside mobile app and record your video on your phone.</li>
            <li>Let it upload to the cloud, then open it in the Riverside browser app for final edits.</li>
            <li>Use the export window to post to Instagram and TikTok, schedule it, and send it to YouTube.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="tip"><strong>Tip: set up a Magic Episodes template once.</strong> Pick your captions template and turn on pause and filler word removal, smooth cuts, fluff finder, and Magic Audio. After that, every new recording gets cleaned up before you even start editing.</p>
          <a href={RIVERSIDE_URL} class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer sponsored">Try Riverside free</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card">
          <h3>Beehiiv</h3>
          <p>Where the emails go. It's where I run my own newsletter. Free up to 2,500 subscribers.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Create a free account and name your newsletter.</li>
            <li>Make one simple signup page and put that link in your bio.</li>
            <li>Write a short welcome email so new people hear from you right away.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>When you go paid, use code <strong class="coupon">REDEFINE</strong> at checkout for 20% off your first 3 months.</p>
          <a href={BEEHIIV_URL} class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer sponsored">Try Beehiiv free &rarr;</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card">
          <h3>Grok Bot</h3>
          <p>My AI assistant for the thinking part. Hooks, outlines, calls to action, titles, and tags.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open a new chat and tell it who your audience is in one or two lines.</li>
            <li>Paste your brain dump.</li>
            <li>Use the prompts below. Keep what sounds like you. Toss the rest.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-card">
          <h3>Meta Business Suite and Muse (optional)</h3>
          <p>I used Meta Muse only for Facebook and Instagram. It's handy for scheduling and republishing reels. It also gave me strategy and content ideas tied to news and trends related to my videos. Nice to have, not required.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Connect your Facebook Page and Instagram account in Meta Business Suite.</li>
            <li>Schedule or republish a reel from the planner.</li>
            <li>Ask Muse for content ideas tied to what's in the news for your topic.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h2>Use AI to speed it up</h2>
        <p>Copy, paste, fill in the brackets. These work in Grok Bot or any AI assistant.</p>

        <p class="prompt-label">0. Help me pick my niche</p>
        <pre class="prompt">I want to start a 60-day short video challenge. Here are my hobbies, interests, and things I know from work or life: [list]. Suggest 3 niches I could talk about every day for 60 days. For each, give me 5 video ideas and who it's for. Then tell me which one you'd pick for me and why.</pre>

        <p class="prompt-label">1. Brain dump to hooks</p>
        <pre class="prompt">Here's my raw brain dump for a short video: [paste]. My audience is [who]. Give me 3 hook options for the first 3 seconds. Plain language, under 12 words each, no hype. Tell me which one you'd pick and why.</pre>

        <p class="prompt-label">2. Talking points and outline</p>
        <pre class="prompt">Using this hook: [hook]. Pick the 2 or 3 strongest talking points from my brain dump and turn them into a 30 to 60 second outline. Short sentences. Sound like a regular person talking, not a script.</pre>

        <p class="prompt-label">3. One short call to action</p>
        <pre class="prompt">Write one short call to action for the end of this video. Under 8 words. Low key. It should point people to my email list, link in bio. Give me 3 versions.</pre>

        <p class="prompt-label">4. Titles, descriptions, and tags per platform</p>
        <pre class="prompt">Here's the transcript of my video: [paste]. Write a title, a short description, and tags for YouTube, plus a caption with a few hashtags for TikTok and for Instagram. Keep it plain. No clickbait.</pre>

        <p class="prompt-label">5. Repurpose a video into a caption or post</p>
        <pre class="prompt">Turn this video transcript into a short text post for Facebook or Instagram: [paste]. Keep the main point, cut the filler, and end with the same short call to action.</pre>

        <h2>What I'd tell you before you start</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Done beats polished. Post the thing.</li>
          <li>Same routine every day. Fewer decisions means you keep going.</li>
          <li>Keep the ask tiny.</li>
          <li>Get the email. That's the part you own.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If you want the bigger picture on why the list matters, grab my free <a href={PLAYBOOK_URL}>Gen eXit Playbook</a>.</p>

        <p><strong>Want help setting this up for your own thing? Reply to any of my emails and we'll find a time.</strong></p>

        <p>Talk soon,<br />Corey</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .ty-container { max-width: 720px; text-align: center; }
  .ty-cover { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 220px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem; border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.16); transform: rotate(-2deg); }
  .ty-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .ty-headline { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.6rem); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.15; }
  .ty-subhead { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .vt-body { padding-top: 0; }
  .disclosure { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-light); font-style: italic; }
  .side-note {
    margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--blue); background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }
  .side-note-label, .prompt-label {
    font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--text-light); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .prompt-label { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .tool-card {
    margin: 1.5rem 0; padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: #fff;
  }
  .tool-card h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .tool-card ol { margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .tool-card .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; }
  /* .prose a (global) outranks .btn; force white text on pink CTA buttons (#DB2777 ≈4.9:1, hover #BE185D ≈6.4:1) */
  .tool-card a.btn,
  .tool-card a.btn:link,
  .tool-card a.btn:visited,
  .tool-card a.btn:hover,
  .tool-card a.btn:focus,
  .tool-card a.btn:active { color: #fff; text-decoration: none; }
  .prompt {
    white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6; background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .tip { background: var(--bg-subtle); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .coupon { color: var(--text); }
</style>
